  "uprn": "100023402797",
  "decision_date": "23/10/2009",
  "description": "Demolition of existing day centre and erection of a four-storey building comprising new day centre at ground floor, with 19 two-bedroom units on floors 1-3, incorporating a roof terrace/garden and associated parking and landscaping.",
  "site_name": "741",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "11/08/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "08/12/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 08.00 to 18.00 on Mondays to Friday, 08.00 to 13.00 on Saturdays and none on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external and internal noise shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscaping and lighting have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Such details shall include, trees to be retained, boundary treatment, parking layouts, vehicle access, separate pedestrian access and planting plans, and the scheme shall not be implemented otherwise than in accordance with any approval given. The details so approved shall be implemented before first occupation of the properties or (in the case of planting ) in the first available planting season after completion of the development.",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before any part of the building  is occupied or in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 9 - In this condition \"retained tree\" means an existing tree which is to be retained in accordance with the approved plans and particulars; and paragraphs (a) and (b) below shall have effect until the expiration of (5 years?) from (the date of the occupation of the building for its permitted use).\r\n\r\n(a)\tNo retained tree shall be cut down, uprooted or destroyed, nor shall any retained tree be topped or lopped other than in accordance with the approved plans and particulars, without the written approval of the local planning authority.  Any topping or lopping approved shall be carried out in accordance with British Standard[3998 (Tree Work)] or any other BS replacing.\r\n\r\n(b)\tIf any retained tree is removed, uprooted or destroyed or dies, another tree shall be planted at the same place and that tree shall be of such size and species, and shall be planted at such time, as may be specified in writing by the local planning authority.\r\n\r\n(c)\tThe erection of fencing for the protection of any retained tree shall be undertaken in accordance with the approved plans and particulars before any equipment, machinery or materials are brought on to the site for the purposes of the development, and shall be maintained until all equipment, machinery and surplus materials have been removed from the site.  Nothing shall be stored or placed in any area fenced in accordance with this condition and the ground levels within those areas shall not be altered, nor shall any excavation be made, without the written consent of the local planning authority.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before development commences details of sightlines at the point of access to the public highway shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall be carried out in accordance with the details.",
    "Condition : 11 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 12 - The self-contained ground floor office, on the western side of the building (shown on drawing number 03/337 P102C) shall only be occupied by a voluntary organisation serving the local community, and shall not be used for any other purpose unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 13 - The proposed redevelopment of the site for housing with replacement day centre would be compatible with the character of the area and the proposal would not harm the appearance of the street scene or neighbours' living conditions. The development would provide acceptable living conditions, and a community facility and would accord with the Council's traffic and parking standards. The proposal complies with adopted Unitary Development Plan policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), C.1.3 (Existing social and community facilities), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.4.2 (Residential Density) and T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities For Developments)."
  ],
